# ── Production (Vercel) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real values live in Vercel > Project (webwithirfan) > Settings >
# Environment Variables. They are injected at build time on every deploy.
# Never commit a file containing real values; .gitignore blocks *.env / .env.*.
#
# VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY  — Web3Forms access key (https://web3forms.com), created
#                       for info@webwithirfan.com. Set it for the Production
#                       environment (add Preview too if preview deploys should
#                       send real emails). The key is public by design and
#                       ships in the client bundle, but keep it out of git so
#                       rotating it stays a one-place change.
#                       Recipients: primary info@webwithirfan.com, with
#                       mirfanawan545@gmail.com as CC (configured in the
#                       Web3Forms dashboard for this key).
# VITE_SITE_URL       — public site origin, used for canonical/OG URLs.
#
# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (a name Vite actually loads; `local.env` is
# NOT read by Vite) and paste the key:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# With no key set the contact form falls back to a prefilled mailto:, so local
# dev works without one — you just will not exercise the real Web3Forms path.

VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
VITE_SITE_URL=https://webwithirfan.com
